  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (Bachelor of Arts in Psychology, Bachelor of Arts in Social and Criminal Justice, and a truncated Bachelor of Arts in Social Science). This ledger assumes Psychology was the intended program; please confirm.",
    "Block totals (33 Global Campus Foundations + 39 major + 54 electives = 126) exceed 120 because 6 major credits also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements. PSY 101 and MAT 232 are marked as satisfying Foundations requirements. The capture does not say which Foundations slots they replace, so the itemized ledger sums to 126 rather than 120.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations courses are the 'standard' sequence and 'Courses may be substituted'. The allowed substitutions are not listed in the capture.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled as the first course and satisfies 3 elective credits. GEN 104 is scheduled for students transferring fewer than 30 credits and also satisfies 3 elective credits. Both draw from the 54-credit elective block rather than adding credits.",
    "PSY 350 may be replaced by PSY 361 (3 credits), per the printed 'OR PSY 361 (3 credits)'. PSY 361's title is not given in the capture.",
    "Residency requirement: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University. The capture does not tie this to specific courses, so no requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Upper-division requirement: at least 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major. Which courses count as upper-division is not defined in the capture.",
    "Graduation also requires a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University.",
    "Prerequisites (e.g., Quantitative Reasoning, PSY 101, PSY 326, MAT 232) affect sequencing but not credit totals. Sequencing details beyond what is printed are not captured."
  ],
